iterations.reply:
I've left out the `http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`, and the fetch would send untrusted feed text to an external host without the node declaring that capability. The output would also stay unchanged, so the call would be a silent outbound channel. Once the graph's `with` clause includes `http-client`, I can add the call, but I'd recommend a fixed, non-untrusted lookup key rather than the item's text.

```wit
package gen:node;

use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item, classification};

world node {
    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(item: feed-item) -> classification;
}
```

